 [>] Http Headers :
     - General headers  => both request and response, describe the message. // Date, Connection ...
     - Entity headers   => both, describe the content. // Content-Type, Media-Type, Content-Length, Content-Encoding, Boundary, etc
     - Request headers  => do not relate to the content. // Host, User-Agent, Cookie 
     - Response headers => do not relate to the content. // Server, Set-Cookie
     - Security headers => used to specify certain rules and policies. // 
     - custom headers maybe..
 [>] cURL :  
        -v   verbose, 
        -I   display only the response headers
        -i   ^ both the headers and response body

